SAR ADC split capacitive DAC, one half, ideal capacitors, 16 codes: the VACASK twin of sar_cdac_half.cir
// specs/analog/decks/vacask_cdac_half.sim -- second-simulator data for specs/analog/vacask_compare.t27 (analog M4a, #10911, epic #10486). A netlist in VACASK's
// own syntax plus a control block; the numbers are read from its raw file (see "What is read").
// Topology of Diff_cap_DAC as in sar_cdac_half.cir (the ngspice deck of this repository, which this deck repeats): the LSB array, 31 units from node l to the
// plates p1..p5 (1, 2, 4, 8, 16 units), the bridge, 1 unit between l and m (m is Vout, the top plate), and the MSB array, 31 units from m to the plates p6..p10
// (1, 2, 4, 8, 16 units). Unit = 100 fF, ideal. VACASK's capacitor device has one value per instance: a plate of u units is ONE capacitor of u * 100 fF (the
// ngspice deck has u of 100 fF; parallel capacitors are one capacitor of the sum). No golden-deck text is used: the topology is the repository's own deck's.
// The tracking switch is not modelled: l and m start at the sampled 0.75 V (icmode "uic" and the ic list; every capacitor starts uncharged because every plate
// rests at VCM = 0.75 V: the ic list names the ten plate nodes too, at 0.75 V, because in uic mode a node that is not listed starts at 0 V, also a node a
// source drives, so a capacitor between l and an unlisted plate would start charged to 0.75 V and shift every result by 0.75 V; the ngspice deck's IC=0 on
// each capacitor says the same thing). The plates rest at 0.75 V for 10 ns; then, over 1 ps, plate j goes to VDD = 1.5 V when bit j-1 of the circuit variable code is 1 and to
// 0 V when it is 0 (the ngspice deck's 0.75 + 0.75 (2 bit - 1)): the code is `code`. The network is algebraic (capacitors only), so the settled voltage does not
// depend on the time grid. Sweep "cs" (analysis cdac): the 16 codes of the spec's NG_SPOT list. Integration: trapezoidal (VACASK's default), the step capped at 1 ns,
// stop at 30 ns.
// What is read (outside this file, from cdac.raw): v(m) and v(l) at 29 ns, interpolated linearly between the two nearest points. Run: vacask -sp -qp
// vacask_cdac_half.sim     (cwd holds nothing else; only the OSDI file capacitor.osdi of VACASK's own device library is loaded).

load "capacitor.osdi"
model v vsource
model cap capacitor

cl1 (l p1) cap c=100f
cl2 (l p2) cap c=200f
cl3 (l p3) cap c=400f
cl4 (l p4) cap c=800f
cl5 (l p5) cap c=1600f
cbr (l m) cap c=100f
cm6 (m p6) cap c=100f
cm7 (m p7) cap c=200f
cm8 (m p8) cap c=400f
cm9 (m p9) cap c=800f
cm10 (m p10) cap c=1600f
vp1 (p1 0) v type="pwl" wave=[0, 0.75, 10n, 0.75, 10.001n, 0.75+0.75*(2*fmod(floor(code*1.0/1), 2)-1)]
vp2 (p2 0) v type="pwl" wave=[0, 0.75, 10n, 0.75, 10.001n, 0.75+0.75*(2*fmod(floor(code*1.0/2), 2)-1)]
vp3 (p3 0) v type="pwl" wave=[0, 0.75, 10n, 0.75, 10.001n, 0.75+0.75*(2*fmod(floor(code*1.0/4), 2)-1)]
vp4 (p4 0) v type="pwl" wave=[0, 0.75, 10n, 0.75, 10.001n, 0.75+0.75*(2*fmod(floor(code*1.0/8), 2)-1)]
vp5 (p5 0) v type="pwl" wave=[0, 0.75, 10n, 0.75, 10.001n, 0.75+0.75*(2*fmod(floor(code*1.0/16), 2)-1)]
vp6 (p6 0) v type="pwl" wave=[0, 0.75, 10n, 0.75, 10.001n, 0.75+0.75*(2*fmod(floor(code*1.0/32), 2)-1)]
vp7 (p7 0) v type="pwl" wave=[0, 0.75, 10n, 0.75, 10.001n, 0.75+0.75*(2*fmod(floor(code*1.0/64), 2)-1)]
vp8 (p8 0) v type="pwl" wave=[0, 0.75, 10n, 0.75, 10.001n, 0.75+0.75*(2*fmod(floor(code*1.0/128), 2)-1)]
vp9 (p9 0) v type="pwl" wave=[0, 0.75, 10n, 0.75, 10.001n, 0.75+0.75*(2*fmod(floor(code*1.0/256), 2)-1)]
vp10 (p10 0) v type="pwl" wave=[0, 0.75, 10n, 0.75, 10.001n, 0.75+0.75*(2*fmod(floor(code*1.0/512), 2)-1)]

control
  var code=0
  save v(m) v(l)
  sweep cs variable="code" values=[0, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 512, 511, 513, 341, 682, 1023] continuation=0
    analysis cdac tran step=1n stop=30n maxstep=1n icmode="uic" ic={"l", 0.75, "m", 0.75, "p1", 0.75, "p2", 0.75, "p3", 0.75, "p4", 0.75, "p5", 0.75, "p6", 0.75, "p7", 0.75, "p8", 0.75, "p9", 0.75, "p10", 0.75}
endc
